#import "release.typ": release, plain-words, signing
#show: release.with(
  title: "Volunteer Agreement and Code of Conduct",
  intro: [*Welcome to the crew!* This is the agreement between you and Sun Brewed Homestead Inc. ("the Homestead"), a California nonprofit public benefit corporation, about what we can expect of each other. Please read all of it and ask a Steward about anything unclear before you sign. Below, "I" means you.],
  details: ("Emergency contact (name)", "Emergency contact phone"),
)

#plain-words[
- You're a volunteer, not an employee. You can stop, or say no to any task, at any time.
- We'll show you how to do things safely. Follow safety instructions, and report any injury the same day.
- Treat everyone with respect, and keep children safe: never be alone with a child who isn't yours.
- Don't speak, spend or promise anything for the Homestead unless a Steward says so.
]

*1. Volunteer status.* I volunteer freely, for civic and charitable reasons, without promise or expectation of pay or benefits. I am not an employee, and nothing I receive (training, meals, produce, pre-approved expense reimbursement) is wages. I understand the Homestead does not provide workers' compensation or health insurance for volunteers unless it tells me so in writing. Either of us may end my volunteering at any time, for any reason.

*2. The Homestead's part.* The Homestead will give me a safety briefing, show me how to do each task before I do it, never pressure me into a task I am not comfortable with, and listen when I raise a concern. I may say no to any task, or stop, at any time.

*3. How I treat people.* I will treat everyone at the Homestead with respect. I will not harass, bully, threaten or discriminate against anyone, including on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, disability, age, national origin or any other status the law protects. I will raise problems with a Farm Lead or Steward rather than escalate them.

*4. Keeping young people safe.* I will not be alone and out of sight with a minor who is not my own child; another adult will be present or within view. I will not contact minors privately (including online) about Homestead matters except through their parent. If my role involves regular contact with minors, I will complete mandated-reporter training and a background check as California law (AB 506) requires, and I will report suspected abuse as that law requires.

*5. Safety, animals and tools.* I will follow safety briefings and instructions from Homestead leads, wear closed-toe shoes, use only tools I have been shown how to use, and report every injury, near miss or hazard the same day. I will tell a lead about any condition or allergy that affects my safety. I will not feed, medicate or move the goats, chickens or cats unless a lead has asked me to, and will wash my hands after handling animals, compost or soil. I will not volunteer under the influence of alcohol or drugs.

*6. Representing the Homestead.* I will not speak or post on the Homestead's behalf, spend its money, or make commitments for it unless a Steward has authorized me. I will never post photos of children, or of people who have not agreed to be photographed.

*7. Property and information.* I will look after Homestead tools, animals and property and return them when I finish. I will keep private information private, as described in the Homestead's mutual confidentiality agreement.

*8. Driving.* If I drive for the Homestead, I will hold a valid license and my own auto insurance, which is primary for any accident.

#signing[*9. General.* This agreement works alongside the Homestead's liability waiver, which I sign separately, and does not change it. It is governed by California law. If any part is held unenforceable, the rest remains in effect. I agree to sign electronically, and my electronic signature binds me as if written by hand. *I have read this agreement and had the chance to ask questions about it, and I sign it voluntarily.* In an emergency, the Homestead may contact the person listed below.]
